  "response_text": "It is a bad idea to add an integer priority to the TCB because if these high priority tasks take a large amount of CPU bursts to run, the higher priority tasks can be queued to run before the tasks are finished. This leaves lower priority tasks starved for CPU time as they are never the highest priority task in the TCB. This would mean that only the highest priority task would ever run. Since with priority, no task can ever pre-empt the current running task, the highest priority task would be able to always use all the CPU time.\\n",
